rules.description:
Detects the cloud-metadata SSRF bypass class exploited by CVE-2026-46678 and CVE-2026-25580 in Pydantic AI (and the same technique across agent frameworks that fetch user-controlled URLs): the link-local cloud-metadata IP 169.254.169.254 (hex a9fe:a9fe) is encoded into an alternate form that defeats a raw-IPv4 blocklist but is still routed to the metadata endpoint by the OS / router, exposing short-lived cloud IAM credentials.
Detection covers the distinctive encoded forms of the metadata IP — not generic URLs — so it fires on the bypass payload itself, not on ordinary outbound calls: (a) IPv6 transition forms: 6to4 (2002:a9fe:a9fe::), IPv4-mapped (::ffff:169.254.169.254
    or ::ffff:a9fe:a9fe), NAT64 (64:ff9b::a9fe:a9fe);
(b) integer/hex obfuscations of 169.254.169.254 (decimal 2852039166, hex
    0xa9fea9fe) reaching a fetch/URL context;
(c) explicit CVE-2026-46678 / CVE-2026-25580 exploitation framing.

